CURRENT IMAGERY STRATEGY
========================

The plugin documentation pages reference upstream project pages, papers, and
GitHub repositories for demos and example imagery, with full attribution
recorded in:

  docs/assets/credits.md

Reusing those images for documentation purposes — with citation and license
recall — is a standard fair-use / fair-dealing practice for technical writing
about academic ML work.

For each plugin page, the "Demos & comparisons" section currently links out
to upstream sources. To embed images directly:

1. Pick the desired image from the upstream source.
2. Either:
   (a) Hot-link to the upstream URL with attribution caption, OR
   (b) Mirror the image into the per-plugin directory below with the
       source URL preserved in the file name or alt text.
3. Update the relevant docs/plugins/<plugin>.md page with the markdown image
   embed, plus a one-line caption containing source / authors / year /
   license / paper citation.
4. Ensure the credits page (docs/assets/credits.md) lists the image with
   the same metadata.

When self-generated screenshots are eventually produced from the plugins,
they become preferable for:
- Parameter panel screenshots from a host UI.
- Before/after frames from CC0 or owned plates.
- Workflow JSON node graphs.

Save those into the relevant subdirectory.
